/*
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/max-sum-subarray-of-size-k5313/1




Problem: Maximum Sum Subarray of Size K
Platform: GeeksforGeeks
Difficulty: Easy

Approach:
Use a fixed-size sliding window of size k.

First calculate the sum of the first k elements.
Then slide the window:
remove the old left element → move i
add the new right element → move j

Update maximum sum after every window.

Mistake:
Don't recalculate the whole window every time.
Just remove the element leaving the window and add the new element.

Important:
Fixed window of size k → Sliding Window.

sum = sum - arr[i] + arr[j]

Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
*/
